<title>UK: Staveley unit wins military orders.</title>
<headline>Staveley unit wins military orders.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Engineering group Staveley Industries Plc said on Wednesday that its U.S.-based unit Staveley NDT Technologies had won $7 million of orders from the U.S. military.</p>
<p>In a statement, Stavely said the contracts include a $5 million order for ultrasonic testing equipment from the U.S. Air force.</p>
<p>The remainder of the orders are for metal inspection equipment from the U.S. Army.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
